    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Plain summary"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The printer has not been migrated yet. The physical T300 is still on the restorable Comgrow/Sovol 1.5.2 image with patched Klipper 0.12.0. The repository now contains a reviewed, commissioning-locked mainline candidate, recovery tooling, safety policy, Orca profile rules, and validation tests."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "My recommendation is to treat the current repository state as ready for owner review and recovery preparation, not ready for unattended installation. The next real-world gate is proving the recovery USB and full eMMC backup before any write to the printer."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What changed in the project"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A pinned mainline stack was prepared around Klipper v0.13.0, Moonraker, Mainsail, KlipperScreen, Crowsnest, KAMP line purge, and a bounded timelapse service."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Safety is moved out of fragile slicer start G-code and into a policy layer, an admission scanner, and reviewed lifecycle macros."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hardBreak"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "agentRequest",
                "attrs": {
                  "requestId": "agent-request-3f79607a-357d-45e6-b1ae-b935bac942e6",
                  "kind": "review",
                  "status": "open",
                  "title": "Review g-code safety layer",
                  "instruction": "explain to me why g-code is a fragile place for safety and if moving this layer somewhere different has any downsides.  \n\nI have concerns that since g-code is something produced by slicers the slicers will be expecting these safety features in this layer. is that something we have accounted for?",
                  "resolution": "",
                  "createdAt": "2026-08-05T09:38:26.523Z",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-08-05T09:38:26.523Z"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The OrcaSlicer profile now emits a small contract: object definitions, START_PRINT temperatures, END_PRINT, pause, M600, and optional per-layer timelapse frames."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The Dossier Engine clone is downstream-only on this laptop: it fetches updates, and its push URL is disabled."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The printer GitHub repo was pushed with commit 0590c50, after rebasing onto the remote network-clarification commit."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sign-off position"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Approve the design direction if you agree with the priorities: hardware safety first, reversible recovery first, no hidden firmware updates, no private GerGo redistribution, no hand-edited model meshes, and no printer movement or heat initiated by automation without you physically choosing it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Do not approve physical installation yet unless the recovery checklist, image backup, boot identity checks, and attended commissioning steps are completed in order."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
